From 2ee095dcad421695e076014786db9926378a0f93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashutosh Chaubey <ashutoshchaubey2999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:46:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agent-loop): regenerate a step cut at the output-token
 ceiling

agent-loop config maxTokensRetries (default 0) regenerates a step whose
response stopped at the output-token ceiling up to that many times. Each
cut response is settled as a log-only assistant/attempt followed by an
agent/max-tokens-retry {turn, step, retry, maxRetries, outputTokens}
event, and the step's request is rebuilt from the unchanged history; the
response that finishes becomes the step's assistant/message. When the
budget runs out the last cut response is the step and the turn ends
max-tokens, as without the setting.
